# Environmental variables are loaded from these files at runtime.
# Commit only non-secret values. Secret values stay out of version control.
#
# Public, non-secret variables (safe to commit) — documented with a
# placeholder so a fresh checkout knows what to configure:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL  — the KOVA API base (with trailing path if needed).
#
# Because NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL is a PUBLIC URL (not a secret), it is the one
# frontend env var documented here. The actual production value still has to
# be set in the Vercel project dashboard (Vercel ignores committed env files
# for production builds unless you explicitly promote them). Until then the
# app falls back to the same-origin API URL when served from
# https://kova-shopp.vercel.app.
#
# Secret values that should NEVER be committed (kept in .env.local or Vercel):
#   CLERK_SECRET_KEY
#   CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY  (public, but kept out of the repo by convention)
#   DATABASE_URL           (frontend does not use this — it belongs in kova-api)
#   PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY    (backend only)
#   RESEND_API_KEY         (backend only)
#   CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET  (backend only)

# Public API base URL — set this in Vercel to the deployed KOVA API.
# Local dev overrides this via .env.local (localhost by default).
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=""
